# The fixture directories are checked by byte and by line, so they are pinned to
# LF for the same reason the repository root pins *.go: on Windows git converts
# to CRLF on checkout, and a fixture whose bytes differ between the tree the
# criteria were demonstrated on and the tree a reviewer checks out is a fixture
# that proves something about neither.
#
# The root .gitattributes pins the source and config types the toolchain reads;
# these four are the types only this package's testdata uses. Images are left
# alone — git detects them as binary and converts nothing.
*.html text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.tsv  text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
